# Book Intelligence Collector — Selenium Web Scraping

A Python web scraping project built using Selenium WebDriver to extract, validate, and analyze book information from the [Books to Scrape](https://books.toscrape.com/) practice website.

This project is part of my **Python Practical Journey**, focusing on browser automation, web scraping, data validation, and reliable data extraction.

## Features

- Automates Google Chrome using Selenium WebDriver.
- Extracts book information using CSS selectors.
- Independently extracts the same information using XPath.
- Collects book titles, prices, and availability.
- Stores extracted records in Python lists of dictionaries.
- Checks records for missing fields.
- Compares CSS and XPath extraction results.
- Identifies the most expensive book.
- Detects duplicate book titles using Python sets.
- Reports scraping success or failure based on validation conditions.
- Uses explicit waits and handles Selenium timeout exceptions.
- Closes the browser using a `finally` block.

## Technologies

- Python 3
- Selenium WebDriver
- Google Chrome
- CSS Selectors
- XPath

